<script>
' A minimal Timer-owning leaf, reused by DestroyCustomDemo.thr in two different shapes — closing
' the two "Still open" items in findings/component-unmount-hook.md, which were about ft_unmount
' timing/guarding, not about Timer statements themselves (see findings/timer-statements.md for
' that side):
'
' 1. `cardTicker` — a plain, always-present direct child of `card`, DestroyCustomDemo's own
'    destroy-mode/`out:fade`-transitioning element. Gives that block's own exit-animation-deferred
'    teardown real Timer content, so the interleaving between focus recovery (fires immediately when
'    the exit animation STARTS) and the ft_unmount cascade (fires only once the exit animation STOPS
'    and the destroy sub actually runs) is directly observable via tick evidence, not just "navigation
'    kept working."
' 2. `badgeTicker` — inside its OWN nested `{#if:destroy}` block (`showBadge`) with a LONGER `out:fade`
'    than `card`'s own — deliberately toggled off first, then `card` itself toggled off before
'    `badgeTicker`'s own slower exit animation finishes. `card`'s own (faster) destroy sub's unmount
'    cascade reaches `badgeTicker` directly (it's in `card`'s own flat `nestedIds`, same component,
'    not an opaque cross-component boundary) while `badgeTicker`'s own destroy sub hasn't run yet —
'    exactly the "calling ft_unmount on a node whose own children are already mid-teardown" gap.
'
' Not focusable — DestroyCustomDemo.thr's own `card`/`trigger` already own all focusable content and
' key handling for this demo; this widget is purely an observable tick readout, started explicitly via
' `startDemo()`, the same forwarding convention every other Timer demo in this repo already uses
' (see apps/async-demo's TimerLeafWidget.thr).
scale field width: integer = 340
scale field height: integer = 36
scale state readoutTranslation: object = [8, 6]

state tickCount: integer = 0

derived tickLabel: string = "ticks: " + tickCount.ToStr()

public function startDemo() {
  m.tickTimer = setInterval(function() {
    state tickCount = tickCount + 1
  }, 300)
}
</script>

<component>
<Rectangle id="root" color="0x1A1A1AFF" width="{width}" height="{height}">
  <Label id="readout" text="{tickLabel}" color="0xFFFFFFFF" translation="{readoutTranslation}" />
</Rectangle>
</component>
